WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.930
Carbon compounds rule the globe!

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:12.160
They are present in almost all bits and pieces
that we can see, touch, or smell!

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.350
However, when we say “HYDROCARBONS”, what
does it exactly mean?

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.350
Yes!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.230
In literal terms, we mean compounds made up
of

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.890
Carbon and Hydrogen.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.250
But tell me one thing…

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.339
Are all the carbon compounds only
made up of carbon and hydrogen?

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:31.080
Are there no other atoms that makeup the
compounds?

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.850
If all the compounds will have only hydrogen
and carbon, then every

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.500
compound should have the same or similar properties
right?

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.600
But that does not happen!

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.680
We see a wide variety of properties in the
carbon

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.730
compounds because elements other than carbon
and hydrogen can also be

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.950
present in them.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.710
This gets us to the concept of Functional
Groups!

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.430
Now what could this mean?

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.740
Let
us understand this concept in a simple manner

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.760
by splitting the terms.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.680
The word
GROUPS mean a collection.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.530
That indicates a collection of atoms.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.420
And Functional
means having an important role or function!

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.650
This tells us that the functional group is
a group of atoms that have an extremely

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.130
important role in the FUNCTIONALITY of the
compound that they are present in.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.130
Yes!

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:22.790
Say there is a random compound WXYZ which
is attached to the functional

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.530
group AB.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.200
In this case, the properties of this entire
compound are majorly

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.870
determined by the functional group AB.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:35.230
There’s another way in which we can
understand functional groups.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:39.690
They are defined as the group of atoms which
have definite properties.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.409
These functional groups impart the properties
to the

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:44.810
compound in which they are present.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.840
The presence of functional groups defines
the properties irrespective of the length

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.720
of the principal chain of carbon or side
chains attached to it.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.890
Do we know a few examples of functional groups?

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.700
Of course we do!

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.770
You must have come across the terms “Alcohols”,
“Aldehydes”, “Ketones”,

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.200
“Phenols” and so on!

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.320
These are nothing but functional groups!

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.590
So let us say we take a carbon chain of ten
carbon units.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.620
The carbon chain may be
a straight chain or branched one.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.950
Say it has an alcoholic functional group attached
to it.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.129
This was the case of saturated hydrocarbons.

00:02:22.129 --> 00:02:25.599
Same holds true for unsaturated
hydrocarbons as well.

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:29.469
Now in any case the properties of the compound
formed will depend on two

00:02:29.469 --> 00:02:31.349
factors!

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:36.739
First factor is the presence or absence of
single, double or triple covalent bonds

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:38.950
between the carbon atoms.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:45.810
It means the compound being saturated or
unsaturated will define many of its reactions.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:49.790
Another important influencing factor is the
presence of a functional group.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.779
It is
this group that gives the characteristic properties

00:02:52.779 --> 00:02:55.159
to the compound formed.

00:02:55.159 --> 00:02:59.230
Now let us have a look at a few more examples
of functional groups along with

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.319
their structures in the upcoming videos!

